<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106445" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑδρο-ρρόα</span></b> , ἡ, but in 
			Att.
		 also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑδρορρόη</span> acc. to
			Moer.<i><span class="en">
			p.381
		</span></i> P., and so <i><span class="en">
			Polyaen.
			1.37
		</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥοή</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>water-course,</i> whether on the
			ground, <i>conduit, sluice,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				922
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				1186
			</span></i>; or on the roof, <i>gutter, spout,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>V.</u>
				126
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ τῶν ὀφθαλμῶν ὑδρορρόαι δύο
					ῥέουσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eub.
					98.4
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδρωψ</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				312
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>a hidden rock in the sea,</i> acc. to (the error of) Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				1181
			</span></i>.</div>
